// The boreal forest's own animals (V2-10, the first expansion wave), Palearctic and Nearctic:
// moose and reindeer, the wolverine, the lynx of the snowshoe hare, the mountain hare, the cone
// squirrel, sable and marten, the ermine, the conifer grouse and the jays, the great grey owl.
// Masses, speeds, densities and life histories are rounded values for wild adults from general
// mammal and ornithological references (the Handbook of the Mammals of the World, the Handbook
// of the Birds of the World, species accounts and boreal field studies); daily food is dry
// matter for plant-eaters and fresh meat for hunters. Densities are for good habitat, as the
// temperate species' are: boreal land feeds them at a fraction of it (its production is less).
